@startuml 00-overview
!pragma layout smetana
title Two doors, one equation, three implementations
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #eef4fa
  BorderColor #4a7ebb
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #fffbe6
  BorderColor #d6c36b
}

rectangle "**Source System**\nfull snapshot, once per run" as SRC
rectangle "**intake**\nparse door" as INT
rectangle "**curate + enrich**\nadds columns, rejects nothing" as CUR
rectangle "**produce**\nmap door · schema door" as PROD
rectangle "**Target System**\nload on Kafka, idempotent" as TGT

SRC -right-> INT
INT -right-> CUR
CUR -right-> PROD
PROD -right-> TGT

note bottom of PROD
  **written** → becomes a target document
  **rejected** → named, with an enumerated reason
  `src_read = written + rejected`
  a run that does not balance **fails**
end note

rectangle "**spec/PIPELINE.md**\nthe one definition" as SPEC
rectangle "**implementations/**\nBeam/Dataflow · Flink · Flink-JDBC" as IMPL
rectangle "**oracle + comparator**\nrow for row, never counts alone" as ORACLE

SPEC -right-> IMPL
IMPL -right-> ORACLE

note bottom of ORACLE
  same spec, several implementations:
  conformance means the same everywhere
end note
@enduml